# record points at the VPS's IP. Caddy then provisions and auto-renews a
# real Let's Encrypt certificate on first request -- nothing else to
# configure for HTTPS.
#
# No domain yet? Point this at the VPS's bare IP instead (e.g. "1.2.3.4")
# -- Caddy serves plain HTTP for an IP address (it can't get a public cert
# for one) so you're not blocked on DNS, but switch to a real domain before
# putting real documents through this.

